  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia - World Bank Indonesia Partnership (ABIP) Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia-World Bank Indonesia Partnership Phase 2 (ABIP2) is a country-level, single donor trust fund that provides a platform for the majority of DFAT-funded World Bank activities in Indonesia. ABIP&#x2019;s goal is to support the Government of Indonesia&#x2019;s efforts to increase inclusive economic growth across four thematic areas, including the promotion of gender equality and climate change initiatives by (i) accelerating human capital development, (ii) improving economic management and prosperity, (iii) building more and better infrastructure, and (iv) promoting sustainable development for a livable planet. The core modalities of the partnership are analytical and policy advisory support, knowledge exchange, support to the World Bank lending operations, and institutional strengthening. ABIP2 will continue to build on the strategic collaboration established between the Bank in Indonesia and DFAT and the coordination with DFAT&#x2019;s bilateral investments.</narrative>
  </description>
